1
00:03:57,692 --> 00:04:03,692
The past is not what it seems.

2
00:07:55,384 --> 00:08:01,384
Frozen II is a family, animation, adventure film directed by Jennifer Lee.

3
00:11:53,076 --> 00:11:59,076
Elsa, Anna, Kristoff and Olaf head far into the forest to learn the
truth about an ancient mystery of their kingdom.

4
00:15:50,769 --> 00:15:56,769
Elsa (voice), played by Idina Menzel.

5
00:19:48,461 --> 00:19:54,461
Anna (voice), played by Kristen Bell.

6
00:23:46,153 --> 00:23:52,153
Olaf (voice), played by Josh Gad.

7
00:27:43,846 --> 00:27:49,846
Kristoff / Sven / Reindeers (voice), played by Jonathan Groff.

8
00:31:41,538 --> 00:31:47,538
Iduna (voice), played by Evan Rachel Wood.

9
00:35:39,230 --> 00:35:45,230
Mattias (voice), played by Sterling K. Brown.

10
00:39:36,923 --> 00:39:42,923
Frozen 2, stylized as Frozen II, is a 2019 American animated musical
fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.

11
00:43:34,615 --> 00:43:40,615
The second film in the Frozen franchise, following the 2013 film, it was directed by Chris Buck and Jennifer Lee and
written by Lee, from a story they conceived with Marc Smith, Kristen Anderson-Lopez, and Robert Lopez.

12
00:47:32,307 --> 00:47:38,307
It stars the voices of Kristen Bell, Idina Menzel, Josh Gad, and Jonathan Groff.

13
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Set three years after the events of the first film, Frozen 2 follows sisters Anna and Elsa, and their companions
Kristoff, Sven, and Olaf as they travel to an enchanted forest to unravel the origin of Elsa's magical power.

14
00:55:27,692 --> 00:55:33,692
Frozen 2 was greenlit in March 2015 after a company debate about
whether it would be perceived as inferior to the original.

15
00:59:25,384 --> 00:59:31,384
It used more-complex, enhanced animation technology compared to the
first film, and was an interdepartmental collaboration.

16
01:03:23,076 --> 01:03:29,076
Anderson-Lopez and Lopez returned as the film's songwriters,
and Christophe Beck again composed the score.

17
01:07:20,769 --> 01:07:26,769
The film was translated into 46 languages and was accompanied by Into
the Unknown: Making Frozen 2, a documentary series.

18
01:11:18,461 --> 01:11:24,461
Frozen 2 premiered in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on November 7, 2019,
and was released in the United States on November 22.

19
01:15:16,153 --> 01:15:22,153
It received generally positive reviews from critics, although
it was considered inferior to its predecessor.

20
01:19:13,846 --> 01:19:19,846
The film grossed $1.450 billion worldwide, finishing its theatrical run as the third-highest-grossing film of 2019,
the tenth-highest-grossing film in history, and the second-highest-grossing animated film of all time.

21
01:23:11,538 --> 01:23:17,538
It also held the title of the highest-grossing worldwide
opening for an animated film for three years.

22
01:27:09,230 --> 01:27:15,230
Frozen 2 received a nomination for Best Original Song at the 92nd
Academy Awards, among numerous other accolades.

23
01:31:06,923 --> 01:31:12,923
A sequel, Frozen 3, is scheduled to be released in 2027.

24
01:35:04,615 --> 01:35:10,615
The film explores themes of princess, magic, kingdom, winter, queen.

25
01:39:02,307 --> 01:39:08,307
The tone is lighthearted.
